            "review_text": "Clement\n1 contribution\n0\nHorrible management follow up\nJun 2022 • Solo\nUsed to dine frequently at their Thao Dien outpost.\n\nOver the years they've been open there, guests have been verbally abusive towards wait staff and no steps are ever taken to manage the toxic or service environment. Staff just take it and allow everyone else to be exposed to it. For context, I averaged 1 to 2 visits per week, situation allowing.\n\nOne of the guests got physical with me and I wrote in to the management and they said their staff can't do anything except call the police even though there are security on the compound that their founder who responded to the email, Jerome seems to have no inkling of. \n\nIn the email I also mentioned that customers are frequently toxic and nothing is being done and he didn't even acknowledge.\n\nAfter writing in again one more time for clarification as to how they handle security and service, they just ghosted my email and when I dmed them on Instagram, Jerome just asks for my phone number to contact me and ghosts me as well.\n\nOne time water was leaking all over the floor from a faulty refrigerator and I had to be the one to remind the staff to clean it up because none of them could be bothered even after half an hour of puddling.\n\nTheir communication generally tends to revolve around their passionate baking and I don't doubt that. But the rhetoric around baking should never detract from the fact it takes way more than just good baking to be a respectable F&B institution and place of service.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten August 5, 2022",
